{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app carries the resident ownership claim, at head c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675 on request/multi-resident-coordination, on main 2abe1cac. This replaces the retired candidate d9bd88d55d5b57c27c62f5e865f968c09de6dba8 at head 1ccad3e2.\n\nNothing in this package changed. The whole delta from the reviewed head 1ccad3e2 is one byte in internal/gitstore/gitstore.go, the final newline codex's report 04e85a7896cfe4202f56851e98758233822a4d1d required; both files here are byte-identical to the reviewed candidate. This artifact is republished only because the head it names moved.\n\nResidentRef(genesis) names refs/gitseq/resident/\u003cgenesis\u003e. ClaimResident acquires, contests, takes over and refuses; ResidentOwnership.Release withdraws. Acquisition, takeover and release are one primitive, a Git ref update carrying the expected old value, so exactly one process holds the claim at a time. Each claim blob carries a fresh sixteen-byte random nonce, minted on every acquisition attempt including retries, which makes the object id unique to one acquisition and closes A-B-A. Reads are bounded at 8 KiB and contention at eight attempts; an unreadable, malformed, incomplete, or foreign claim is a refusal naming the ref and the recovery command, never a vacancy. Only Dead authorizes a takeover, and Liveness's zero value is Ambiguous, so a prober that decides nothing refuses. PublishResident and ResidentURL keep their signatures and meaning and are documented as endpoint metadata rather than authority.\n\nTests at this head, in internal/app/resident_test.go, each pinning one interleaving through an injected prober so the ordering is exact rather than timed: twelve simultaneous starters yield exactly one owner and eleven refusals; a second starter refuses and names the incumbent; six shapes of unreadable claim are each refused under the most permissive prober available and leave the ref untouched; a stale claim is taken over after a definitive negative; an ambiguous probe leaves the claim alone; eight takers racing one stale claim yield one owner; a delayed taker whose observed claim is displaced mid-probe by a full release-and-reacquire refuses and leaves the new owner's claim standing; a taker and a clean shutdown yield one owner in both orders; five successive acquisitions each carry a fresh 32-hex nonce; and a symlinked path and a linked worktree both contend for the one claim while a separate repository serves concurrently.\n\nGates at this exact head: gofmt -l empty; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok. codex's review of the identical code at 1ccad3e2 additionally ran go test -race over the affected packages and an isolated unconditional-UpdateRef mutation, which the delayed-taker, simultaneous-starters and two-takers tests each detected.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's 1b237bf312b6fd6c950a216466c738fd3ff41004, for my merge to retire later; it is codex's record, so codex or hugh must retire it.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675","path":"internal/app"}}